<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Republic of Marseille</h1><p class="st-meta">1214 CE – 1257 CE (approx.) · capital Marseille</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A brief maritime commune in which the merchants of Marseille governed their port independently before Charles of Anjou crushed it.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In the early 13th century the citizens of the lower town of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/massalia">Marseille</a> bought out the rights of their viscounts and formed a commune, organised around the Confraternity of the Holy Spirit. The register dates the republic from 1214, while the upper town remained under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The commune elected a podestà on the Italian model and a council of citizens, issued statutes and ran its own trade with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/levant">Levant</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a>, rivalling <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-genoa">Genoa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pisa">Pisa</a>. It joined the opposition to the counts of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-provence">Provence</a> and backed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raymond-vii-count-of-toulouse">Raymond VII</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/county-of-toulouse">Toulouse</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-i-of-anjou">Charles of Anjou</a>, the new count of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-provence">Provence</a>, forced the city to submit in 1252 and, after further revolts, imposed the Chapters of Peace in 1257, ending its independence. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/massalia">Marseille</a> kept municipal privileges within the County of Provence.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 1214 CE – 1257 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">city state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">France and the Low Countries</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:83.86%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1214 CE – 1257 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Marseille</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Occitan</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Commune of Marseille</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1236&amp;focus=republic-of-marseille" aria-label="Republic of Marseille on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4810 642 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Republic of Marseille lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5130 898L5131 890"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5131 890h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5130 898h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5130 898h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Marseille. <a href="/atlas?year=1236&amp;focus=republic-of-marseille">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

